\fs28\b Phase 2 Code and Test Evidence Audit\b0\par
\fs22 Governance Hub - audit evidence report\par
Audit date: 26 November 2026 UTC\par
Project: /Users/ploggvn/Documents/ai-decision-governance-service\par
Primary application: ChatGPT Library Phase_2_Application_Governance_Hub_Revised.docx (libfile_3ad26b9be7888191b4c8a0e00cdba846)\par
\par
\fs26\b Executive summary\b0\par
The repository is a Next.js/TypeScript frontend proof of concept with synthetic data and local browser workflows. It is not a deployed AI governance backend. No FastAPI service, PostgreSQL database, migrations, Docker/Compose files, OIDC/RBAC/ABAC implementation, provider connector, webhook receiver or real AI telemetry producer was found.\par
\par
Static evidence passed: production build, TypeScript, 16 domain tests, 34 monitoring tests, 60 token-level contrast pairs, formatting and monitoring contract generation. Playwright discovered 113 authored tests, but runtime execution was blocked by repeated EMFILE file-watcher errors. No browser test or screenshot is counted as passed.\par
\par
\fs26\b Current inventory\b0\par
15 business routes are declared. Seed data contains 8 AI systems, 3 policies, 5 requirements, 6 assessments, 3 evidence records, 3 remediation tasks and 3 audit records. Governance persistence is localStorage. The monitoring default is a browser-timer demo; its live REST/SSE client is only an adapter contract and has no server in this repository.\par
\par
\fs26\b Requirement evidence\b0\par
E1: policy impact and reassessment are represented by a local queue workflow, not a versioned policy/control graph or backend impact engine.\par
E2: typed REST/OpenAPI/SSE client code exists, but no API producer, connector, webhook, ingestion or synchronization service exists.\par
E3: workspace switching is UI/localStorage filtering; authentication, authorization, RLS, residency, retention, deletion and legal hold are absent.\par
E4: five frontend outcomes exist as compliant, partial, noncompliant, insufficient and NA; separate UNKNOWN, framework source anchors, certainty and versioned controls are absent.\par
E5: local reviewer rationale and audit rows exist; durable authorization and immutable server history are absent.\par
E6: synthetic latency/error/request metrics exist; evaluator datasets, baselines, thresholds and reproducible data/model/output risk assessments are absent.\par
A1: no deployment artifacts. A2: bilingual UI data exists, rendered verification blocked. A3: synthetic local tenants only. A4: CSV and simulated integrations only; no ticket/webhook notification delivery.\par
\par
\fs26\b Synthetic E1 evidence\b0\par
An isolated fixture was added at docs/audit/evidence/synthetic/policy-change-365-to-90-fixture.json. It contains SYS-A in scope, SYS-B/SYS-C out of scope, policy P-01 changing from 365 to 90 days and valid evidence 120 days old. Its oracle is affected SYS-A, unaffected SYS-B/SYS-C, new NOT_MET and historical snapshot preserved. A standalone arithmetic check matched the oracle. The result file explicitly says it was not executed against a product backend.\par
\par
\fs26\b Test results\b0\par
Domain: 16/16 passed. Monitoring: 34/34 passed. Contrast: 60/60 passed. TypeScript and production build passed. OpenAPI contract generation passed. Playwright: 113 listed; runtime blocked and therefore not passed.\par
\par
\fs26\b TRL and submission conclusion\b0\par
The repository supports a frontend proof-of-concept claim and isolated synthetic logic evidence. It does not support a verified TRL 5 claim. The official challenge requires Phase 2 proposals to be in TRL 5-9 and to provide R&D/feasibility evidence. Before submission, implement and verify a backend vertical slice, tenant security, evidence provenance, two connectors, the policy-change scenario, browser/runtime evidence and a controlled simulated validation.\par
\par
\fs26\b Priority next steps\b0\par
P0: FastAPI/PostgreSQL/OIDC/RBAC foundation; versioned policy-control graph and impact API; evidence artifact service; controlled TRL evidence package.\par
P1: connector sandboxes, risk evaluator, durable reviewer revisions, bilingual reports and runnable browser/axe matrix.\par
P2: portable deployment evidence, competitive benchmarks and company-confirmed staffing/IP/funding documentation.\par
\par
Detailed Markdown reports and raw evidence are in docs/audit/. The original application Word document was not modified.\par
